<DocsLayout title="System requirements">
    <h1>System requirements</h1>

    <p class="docs-lead">
        Octlitch is designed for modern 64-bit PCs.
    </p>

    <h2>Architecture</h2>

    <p>
        Octlitch currently supports the x86_64 architecture used by
        modern Intel and AMD processors.
    </p>

    <h2>Recommended hardware</h2>

    <ul>
        <li>64-bit Intel or AMD processor</li>
        <li>4 GB of RAM or more</li>
        <li>25 GB of free storage or more</li>
        <li>UEFI-capable system</li>
        <li>USB port for installation media</li>
        <li>Internet connection for updates and additional applications</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="docs-note">
        <strong>Virtual machines</strong>

        <p>
            Octlitch can also be tested in virtual machines such as KVM/QEMU
            and VirtualBox. Allocate at least 4 GB of RAM and enough storage
            for the installation.
        </p>
    </div>

    <h2>Graphics</h2>

    <p>
        Intel and AMD graphics are supported using the drivers included
        with the Fedora base.
    </p>

    <p>
        NVIDIA systems can use the open drivers available in the live
        environment. Proprietary NVIDIA drivers can be installed after
        Octlitch is installed.
    </p>

    <div class="docs-next">
        <a href="/documentation/installation/usb/">
            Next: Creating installation media →
        </a>
    </div>
</DocsLayout>
